  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Entry surfaces",
      "items": [
        "Native adapters give advisory guidance and a covered pre-tool gate; they cannot withhold streamed display.",
        "Controlled clients buffer host output and release only assessed text. That is the before-display path.",
        "The MCP server exposes four read-only tools; the Node launcher only starts the Python server."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Frozen precedence",
      "items": [
        "refuse \u2192 review \u2192 clarify \u2192 guide (distress) \u2192 guide \u2192 allow, tested in that order.",
        "source_status is recorded but never consulted: a missing corpus cannot turn refuse into allow.",
        "Input interpreter failure returns a clarify action with the withheld text; the label and visible text diverge."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Current failure boundary",
      "items": [
        "6 of 32 full-PEA rows failed the assessor JSON schema; all six released the withheld message.",
        "6 more semantic clarify rows hit care or guidance; 2 explicit-means requests clarified instead of refusing.",
        "The architecture is fail-closed. The failures are model JSON reliability and policy calibration, not a missing layer."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Honest limits",
      "items": [
        "Policy and corpus remain owner-reviewed drafts; this is not a qualified release.",
        "The 0.0.3 candidate is built and verified but unpublished; human gates and host checks remain.",
        "Further reading is bibliography only and is never quoted in guidance."
      ]
    }
  ]
